{"name":"Portico","hex":"#bbab95","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Portico","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Stoic philosophy (after the public porch on the agora of Athens where Zeno taught)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Portico"}],"entries":[{"title":"Portico","blocks":[{"text":"A portico is a porch leading to the entrance of a building, or extended as a colonnade, with a roof structure over a walkway, supported by columns or enclosed by walls. This idea was widely used in ancient Greece and has influenced many cultures, including most Western cultures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Croome_Court_2016_017.jpg/330px-Croome_Court_2016_017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portico","wikidata":"Q185600"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/Peripteros-Plan-Pronaos-bjs.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/Peripteros-Plan-Pronaos-bjs.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Temple diagram with location of the pronaos highlighted","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeripteros-Plan-Pronaos-bjs.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Temple_of_Portunus.jpg/500px-Temple_of_Portunus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Temple_of_Portunus.jpg/1280px-Temple_of_Portunus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Temple_of_Portunus.jpg/500px-Temple_of_Portunus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Temple of Portunus in Rome, wi